keyd-belgian-windows (0.9.2) noble; urgency=medium

  * No functional change; version kept equal to belgian-azerty-windows,
    whose be-azerty-fix can now switch keyd off (Linux-standard profile).
    The service stays off across package updates, which only restart keyd
    when it is enabled.

 -- @MAINTAINER@  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0000

keyd-belgian-windows (0.9.1) noble; urgency=medium

  * systemd drop-in: Restart=always and SuccessExitStatus=2 15, so that
    "systemctl stop keyd" ends as inactive instead of failed (keyd exits
    with status 15 on SIGTERM), while keyd is still restarted when anything
    else stops it.

 -- @MAINTAINER@  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 09:00:00 +0000

keyd-belgian-windows (0.9.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * First packaged version. Split out of the earlier all-in-one keyd
    2.5.0-0beazerty2 build: the rules now come in their own package on top
    of the distribution's (or a backported) keyd, so a keyd upgrade never
    takes them away.
  * Restart=on-failure for keyd through a systemd drop-in.

 -- @MAINTAINER@  Sat, 24 Oct 2026 03:00:00 +0000
